event: response.output_text.done
data: {"type":"response.output_text.done","sequence_number":39,"item_id":"msg_rec_1","output_index":2,"content_index":0,"text":"**No\u2014ROB RUN currently isn’t playable under Proton because Easy Anti-Cheat blocks it.** I opened GamingOnLinux’s ROB RUN compatibility page: it lists **“Anti-Cheat Status: Broken”**, identifies **Easy Anti-Cheat**, and dates its status update to **November 9, 2026**. ([gamingonlinux.com](https://www.gamingonlinux.com/itemdb/app/76544/rob-run/))\n\nThere’s a useful distinction: a November 9 Steam community report says the game **downloads and boots through Proton on Linux/Steam Deck, but joining is blocked by anti-cheat**. So launching it isn’t the same as being able to play. ([steamcommunity.com](https://steamcommunity.com/app/4262460/discussions/0/564798922323803596/?utm_source=openai))"}

